+# Agent Note: Markdown heading source positions
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-09-markdown-heading-source-positions.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+A document viewer receiving a source-line navigation needs to identify the corresponding rendered heading. Display labels are ambiguous after inline formatting and with repeated headings. Footnotes can place headings in a different DOM order from their source order, while a separate parser can disagree with the renderer's mathematics and other extensions.
+
+## Decision
+
+The public `MarkdownText` primitive accepts the opt-in `headingSource` prop. Its settled renderer exposes the original heading line and UTF-16 offset through `data-md-source-line` and `data-md-source-offset`. The consumer compares these coordinates against the exact `text` it supplied. The out-of-tree Markdown sidebar plugin uses them for enclosing ATX-section navigation.
+
+The renderer remains the owner of Markdown interpretation. Source attributes describe actual ATX and setext nodes, including container and footnote headings. Streaming output and generated footnote chrome omit them. The default is false, preserving ordinary component output. No file access, session state, persisted data, or event protocol is added.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Match display labels.** Inline links and duplicate labels make this ambiguous, and generated content can further change the visible text.
+
+**Parse again in the consumer.** A second grammar can disagree about code fences, mathematics and footnotes, leaving source and rendered heading sequences misaligned.
+
+**Always attach coordinates.** Existing consumers do not need them; an opt-in keeps ordinary and streaming output unchanged.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Consumers can navigate using the same parse that produced their displayed document. Coordinates are meaningful only for the supplied source and settled render. Consumers still own navigation lifetime, cancellation and the choice of which heading forms to target.
+
+The primitive tests cover opt-in source coordinates, CRLF, UTF-16, setext and omission during streaming or default rendering. The Markdown plugin's official Slot assembly tests exercise linked and indented headings, repeated labels, fences, mathematics and reordered footnotes. These automated checks do not establish visual scrolling behavior in a real browser.
